{
	"_doc": "The voice of the Pit: the prologue, run-start / run-end narration, Basecamp return lines and the demon's mid-run mutterings. Pools: prologue (by id), run_start, run_end, basecamp_return, run_mid.",
	"conversations": [
		{
			"id": "prologue",
			"who": "narrator",
			"lines": [
				{
					"text": "Hear the Pit, Sinbound. It speaks to you because nothing else will."
				},
				{
					"text": "Above the Verge, the Archons of the Silver City have ordered a sunrise that will never set. They call it the Last Dawn."
				},
				{
					"text": "When it is fully risen, no shadow will survive in any world. Not under a stone. Not inside a heart. Not here."
				},
				{
					"text": "Already the Pit grows cold. Heaven has strung the Lattice of Grace across the sky, and the souls that should fall to us are caught before they land."
				},
				{
					"text": "The Herald Sariel carries the Dawn on its spear. It descends upon the Verge to set the sky alight."
				},
				{
					"text": "So the Ashen Court tore open the Breach, and sent up the one weapon Heaven cannot keep dead. You."
				},
				{
					"text": "Your sins are heavy, {demon}. Too heavy to stay buried. Every time they kill you, you will fall back here, into the Font, and be made again."
				},
				{
					"text": "Go up. Burn their choirs. Bring down the Herald."
				},
				{
					"text": "And when you are Unmade, as you will be, the Pit will be waiting."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "run_start_first",
			"pool": "run_start",
			"once": true,
			"priority": 10,
			"requires": {
				"max": {
					"runs": 1
				}
			},
			"lines": [
				{
					"text": "The Breach yawns open. Above it lies a world that has forgotten how to be afraid. Remind it."
				}
			]
		},
		{
			"id": "run_start_second",
			"pool": "run_start",
